    "longDescription": "I am developing an app which integrate Stripe as payment, but the user doesn't need the hassle going to Stripe to manage everything, they can do it in the app. So when activating Stripe on testing env it works refer to a screenshot This is what I want, user add info and verify the identity and redirect back to my platform and then boom voila. This works on testing environment but on the next screenshots, it's different instead of landing on this screen, am getting this one as asking me to login, my question is there anything I missed on prod? or what can I do to get onboarding screen without first login into Stripe. Because I don't want the user to interact with Stripe. this is my code <script> import { loadConnectAndInitialize } from \"@stripe/connect-js\"; import { apiDataService } from \"@/services/apiDataService\"; export default { data() { return { stripeState: \"idle\", checkingStripeStatus: true, stripeData: null, stripeClientId: null, loading: false, error: null, }; }, methods: { async getStripeStatus() { this.checkingStripeStatus = true; this.error = null; try { const res = await apiDataService.stripeStatus(); const data = res.data; if (data.is_fully_onboarded) { this.stripeData = data; this.stripeState = \"connected\"; } else if (data.stripe_account_id) { this.stripeData = data; this.stripeClientId = data.stripe_account_id; this.stripeState = \"onboarding\"; await this.$nextTick(); await this.initializeStripeConnect(); } else { this.stripeState = \"idle\"; } } catch (err) { console.error(err); this.error = \"Failed to fetch Stripe status\"; this.stripeState = \"idle\"; } finally { this.checkingStripeStatus = false; } }, async startConnect() { this.loading = true; this.error = null; try { const res = await apiDataService.connectStripe(); const data = res.data; if (data.is_fully_onboarded) { this.stripeData = data; this.stripeState = \"connected\"; return; } if (data.needs_onboarding && data.onboarding_url) { window.location.href = data.onboarding_url; return; } this.stripeClientId = data.account_id; this.stripeState = \"onboarding\"; await this.$nextTick(); await this.initializeStripeConnect(); } catch (err) { console.error(err); this.error = err.response?.data?.error || \"Failed to create Stripe account\"; } finally { this.loading = false; } }, async initializeStripeConnect() { if (!this.$refs.stripeContainer) { console.error(\"Stripe container not found\"); return; } const publishableKey = process.env.VUE_APP_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY; if (!publishableKey) { this.error = \"Stripe publishable key not configured\"; return; } try { this.$refs.stripeContainer.innerHTML = \"\"; const instance = await loadConnectAndInitialize({ publishableKey, fetchClientSecret: async () => { const response = await apiDataService.clientSecretEmbedding({ account_id: this.stripeClientId, }); return response.data.client_secret; }, }); const onboarding = instance.create(\"account-onboarding\"); this.$refs.stripeContainer.appendChild(onboarding); onboarding.addEventListener(\"onboarding_completed\", () => { this.stripeState = \"connected\"; this.getStripeStatus(); }); onboarding.addEventListener(\"onboarding_exited\", () => { this.getStripeStatus(); }); } catch (err) { console.error(\"Stripe error:\", err); this.error = err.message || \"Failed to initialize Stripe onboarding\"; } }, }, mounted() { this.getStripeStatus(); }, }; </script> and for template <div v-if=\"stripeState === 'onboarding'\"> <div ref=\"stripeContainer\"></div> </div> The backend API, It provides: { \"stripe_account_id\": \"acct_xxx\", \"is_fully_onboarded\": false } and a separate endpoint returns the client secret required by loadConnectAndInitialize().",
